<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson says wins $100 mln AXE order.</title>
<headline>Ericsson says wins $100 mln AXE order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Monday it signed an AXE switching agreement worth $100 million with Irish telephone operator Telecom Eireann which will run from 1998 to 2002.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Ericsson will deliver all equipment, support and services associated with the development of the Irish telecommunications network, including network expansion and modernisation programmes, Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
</text>
